        "collapsible_tab_RUBEc8": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Course Detail",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>Our Express Test & Tag Course takes half the amount of time in our classroom as our regular course. It's specially designed for those who value practical, hands-on learning without the time constraints. This basically means more time can be spent with the hands-on learning of the test and tag process.<br/><br/>The theory and OHS aspect of the training is online and includes interactive videos, information and assessments, allowing you to spend as much time as you need to complete this. This usually takes about 3-4 hours for each module and must be completed before attending the practical session.<br/><br/>When it comes to the practical component, you will be shown how to use a PAT Tester in a small-sized class by one of our test and tag expert trainers. This will ensure you have an interactive learning experience and are given all the help you need. All of the training equipment will be provided during this session. The practical section goes for 4 hours, with times available at 8am-12pm and 1pm-5pm.<br/><br/>After the course, you'll receive full lifetime technical support from our team, so if you run into any problems at all, we'll be there to guide you through it.<br/><br/>Please note that the Australian Standard AS/NZS 3760:2022 changed in 2022 and our training course is now teaching the updated Standard.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
